p=3: [xbar,ybar] = [1, 2] (i.e. xbar - ybar); antisymmetric: True; Jacobi: True; gamma_n nonzero for n = 1..6: [True, True, True, True, True, True]
p=5: [xbar,ybar] = [1, 4] (i.e. xbar - ybar); antisymmetric: True; Jacobi: True; gamma_n nonzero for n = 1..6: [True, True, True, True, True, True]
p=7: [xbar,ybar] = [1, 6] (i.e. xbar - ybar); antisymmetric: True; Jacobi: True; gamma_n nonzero for n = 1..6: [True, True, True, True, True, True]
So gamma_{c+1}(A) = gamma_3(A) != 0 (A is not nilpotent): the chart passes a Lie check, fails gamma_{c+1} = 0, and Theorem main (class <= c) is called on it with no rule for that case.
